{"id":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#prop:warped-product-isometry","title":"prop:warped-product-isometry","path":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2.md","line":3848,"body":"","kind":"theorem","status":"not_started","tex":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2.tex#prop:warped-product-isometry","uses":["[[references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#ex:warped-products]]","[[references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#def:polar-map]]","[[references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#lem:mfderiv-polar-map]]","[[references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#lem:sphere-tangent-orthogonal-radius]]","[[references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#def:metric-preserving]]","[[references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#def:open-submanifold-metric]]","[[references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#prop:warped-product-constant-one]]"],"inspired_by":[],"bindings":[],"is_index":false,"body_html":"","formal":[],"tex_content":{"path":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2.tex","label":"prop:warped-product-isometry","line":6589,"source":"\\begin{proposition}\\label{prop:warped-product-isometry}\\dcref{ch2:2-4}\n\n\n\\uses{ex:warped-products,def:polar-map,lem:mfderiv-polar-map,lem:sphere-tangent-orthogonal-radius,def:metric-preserving,def:open-submanifold-metric,prop:warped-product-constant-one}\nFor $\\rho(r)=r$, the map\n$\\Phi:\\mathbb R^+\\times_\\rho S^{n-1}\\to\\mathbb R^n\\setminus\\{0\\}$,\n$\\Phi(\\rho,\\omega)=\\rho\\omega$, is an isometry.\n\\end{proposition}\n\n\\begin{proof}\n\n\\uses{def:polar-map,lem:mfderiv-polar-map,lem:sphere-tangent-orthogonal-radius,def:metric-preserving}\n\\sketch Using Lemma \\ref{lem:mfderiv-polar-map}, the Euclidean pairing of two differentials is\n\\[\naa'+ar\\langle\\omega,d\\iota(w')\\rangle+a'r\\langle d\\iota(w),\\omega\\rangle+r^2\\langle d\\iota(w),d\\iota(w')\\rangle\n=aa'+r^2\\mathring g_\\omega(w,w')\n\\]\nby Lemma \\ref{lem:sphere-tangent-orthogonal-radius}; this is the warped metric. The map is bijective with inverse $x\\mapsto(|x|,x/|x|)$.\n\\end{proof}","html":" <p></p><section class=\"theorem\"><div class=\"theorem-label\">Proposition</div></section><span class=\"tex-label\" id=\"tex-label-70726f703a7761727065642d70726f647563742d69736f6d65747279\"></span><span class=\"tex-source-references\" role=\"list\" style=\"display:block\"><span class=\"tex-dcref\" role=\"listitem\" style=\"display:block\">1. ch2:2-4</span></span><p></p><a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FLeeRiemannian%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2Fchapter2%23ex%3Awarped-products\">↗ ex:warped-products</a> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FLeeRiemannian%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2Fchapter2%23def%3Apolar-map\">↗ def:polar-map</a> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FLeeRiemannian%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2Fchapter2%23lem%3Amfderiv-polar-map\">↗ lem:mfderiv-polar-map</a> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FLeeRiemannian%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2Fchapter2%23lem%3Asphere-tangent-orthogonal-radius\">↗ lem:sphere-tangent-orthogonal-radius</a> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FLeeRiemannian%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2Fchapter2%23def%3Ametric-preserving\">↗ def:metric-preserving</a> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FLeeRiemannian%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2Fchapter2%23def%3Aopen-submanifold-metric\">↗ def:open-submanifold-metric</a> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FLeeRiemannian%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2Fchapter2%23prop%3Awarped-product-constant-one\">↗ prop:warped-product-constant-one</a> For <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$\\rho (r)=r$\">$\\rho (r)=r$</span>, the map <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$\\Phi :\\mathbb R^+\\times _\\rho S^{n-1}\\to \\mathbb R^n\\setminus \\{ 0\\} $\">$\\Phi :\\mathbb R^+\\times _\\rho S^{n-1}\\to \\mathbb R^n\\setminus \\{ 0\\} $</span>, <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$\\Phi (\\rho ,\\omega )=\\rho \\omega $\">$\\Phi (\\rho ,\\omega )=\\rho \\omega $</span>, is an isometry.  <p></p><section class=\"theorem proof\"><div class=\"theorem-label\">Proof</div><p><a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FLeeRiemannian%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2Fchapter2%23def%3Apolar-map\">↗ def:polar-map</a> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FLeeRiemannian%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2Fchapter2%23lem%3Amfderiv-polar-map\">↗ lem:mfderiv-polar-map</a> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FLeeRiemannian%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2Fchapter2%23lem%3Asphere-tangent-orthogonal-radius\">↗ lem:sphere-tangent-orthogonal-radius</a> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FLeeRiemannian%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2Fchapter2%23def%3Ametric-preserving\">↗ def:metric-preserving</a> \\sketch Using Lemma <a class=\"reference tex-ref\" href=\"#node=references%2FLeeRiemannian%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2Fchapter2%23lem%3Amfderiv-polar-map\" data-tex-node=\"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#lem:mfderiv-polar-map\" data-tex-anchor=\"tex-label-6c656d3a6d6664657269762d706f6c61722d6d6170\">19</a>, the Euclidean pairing of two differentials is </p><p><span class=\"math\" data-display=\"true\" data-tex=\"\\[  aa&#x27;+ar\\langle \\omega ,d\\iota (w&#x27;)\\rangle +a&#x27;r\\langle d\\iota (w),\\omega \\rangle +r^2\\langle d\\iota (w),d\\iota (w&#x27;)\\rangle =aa&#x27;+r^2\\mathring g_\\omega (w,w&#x27;)  \\]\">\\[  aa&#x27;+ar\\langle \\omega ,d\\iota (w&#x27;)\\rangle +a&#x27;r\\langle d\\iota (w),\\omega \\rangle +r^2\\langle d\\iota (w),d\\iota (w&#x27;)\\rangle =aa&#x27;+r^2\\mathring g_\\omega (w,w&#x27;)  \\]</span></p><p> by Lemma <a class=\"reference tex-ref\" href=\"#node=references%2FLeeRiemannian%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2Fchapter2%23lem%3Asphere-tangent-orthogonal-radius\" data-tex-node=\"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#lem:sphere-tangent-orthogonal-radius\" data-tex-anchor=\"tex-label-6c656d3a7370686572652d74616e67656e742d6f7274686f676f6e616c2d726164697573\">19</a>; this is the warped metric. The map is bijective with inverse <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$x\\mapsto (|x|,x/|x|)$\">$x\\mapsto (|x|,x/|x|)$</span>. </p><span class=\"qed\" aria-label=\"证毕\" style=\"display:block;text-align:right\">□</span></section>","warnings":["部分 TeX 排版细节未完整还原（已保留可读内容）: sketch"]},"previous":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#lem:mfderiv-polar-map","next":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#prop:grassmann-stiefel-manifolds","relations":[{"kind":"uses","id":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#ex:warped-products","title":"ex:warped-products","label":"ex:warped-products"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#def:polar-map","title":"def:polar-map","label":"def:polar-map"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#lem:mfderiv-polar-map","title":"lem:mfderiv-polar-map","label":"lem:mfderiv-polar-map"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#lem:sphere-tangent-orthogonal-radius","title":"lem:sphere-tangent-orthogonal-radius","label":"lem:sphere-tangent-orthogonal-radius"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#def:metric-preserving","title":"def:metric-preserving","label":"def:metric-preserving"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#def:open-submanifold-metric","title":"def:open-submanifold-metric","label":"def:open-submanifold-metric"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#prop:warped-product-constant-one","title":"prop:warped-product-constant-one","label":"prop:warped-product-constant-one"}],"backlinks":[{"kind":"uses","id":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter10#lem:metric-relation-euclidean","title":"lem:metric-relation-euclidean","label":"lem:metric-relation-euclidean"}],"copy_context":{"version":1,"level":0,"node":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#prop:warped-product-isometry","title":"prop:warped-product-isometry","tex":"\\begin{proposition}\\label{prop:warped-product-isometry}\\dcref{ch2:2-4}\n\n\n\\uses{ex:warped-products,def:polar-map,lem:mfderiv-polar-map,lem:sphere-tangent-orthogonal-radius,def:metric-preserving,def:open-submanifold-metric,prop:warped-product-constant-one}\nFor $\\rho(r)=r$, the map\n$\\Phi:\\mathbb R^+\\times_\\rho S^{n-1}\\to\\mathbb R^n\\setminus\\{0\\}$,\n$\\Phi(\\rho,\\omega)=\\rho\\omega$, is an isometry.\n\\end{proposition}\n\n\\begin{proof}\n\n\\uses{def:polar-map,lem:mfderiv-polar-map,lem:sphere-tangent-orthogonal-radius,def:metric-preserving}\n\\sketch Using Lemma \\ref{lem:mfderiv-polar-map}, the Euclidean pairing of two differentials is\n\\[\naa'+ar\\langle\\omega,d\\iota(w')\\rangle+a'r\\langle d\\iota(w),\\omega\\rangle+r^2\\langle d\\iota(w),d\\iota(w')\\rangle\n=aa'+r^2\\mathring g_\\omega(w,w')\n\\]\nby Lemma \\ref{lem:sphere-tangent-orthogonal-radius}; this is the warped metric. The map is bijective with inverse $x\\mapsto(|x|,x/|x|)$.\n\\end{proof}","source":"tex/references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2.tex","description":"","dependencies":[{"node":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#ex:warped-products","title":"ex:warped-products","description":""},{"node":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#def:polar-map","title":"def:polar-map","description":""},{"node":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#lem:mfderiv-polar-map","title":"lem:mfderiv-polar-map","description":""},{"node":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#lem:sphere-tangent-orthogonal-radius","title":"lem:sphere-tangent-orthogonal-radius","description":""},{"node":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#def:metric-preserving","title":"def:metric-preserving","description":""},{"node":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#def:open-submanifold-metric","title":"def:open-submanifold-metric","description":""},{"node":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#prop:warped-product-constant-one","title":"prop:warped-product-constant-one","description":""}],"dependencies_omitted":0,"unresolved_dependencies":[],"unresolved_omitted":0}}